            <div xml:id="d1247">

                <pb facs="1289" n="1277" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/11–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-13T14:00:00+02:00">November 13,
                            1945—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1450. My 1445, November 12, 4 p.m. In conversation with Prime Minister he asked
                    whether I was satisfied with form of interim reply <pb facs="1290" n="1278"
                        xml:id="pg1278"/> given me by Erkin to our proposal for revision Montreux
                    Convention or whether I would prefer a written reply. I said that Erkin had
                    explained that his statement should be regarded as official interim reply of
                    Turkish Govt pending receipt of views of British and Soviet Govts when a more
                    detailed and presumably written reply would be made. Under these circumstances I
                    said that I personally saw no reason to request any change in form of this
                    interim reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
